klass('ace','ACE inhibitor','Inhibits angiotensin-converting enzyme, reducing angiotensin II and aldosterone while increasing bradykinin.','Avoid in pregnancy and with prior ACE inhibitor-associated angioedema.','Dry cough, hyperkalemia, and angioedema.','Potassium supplements or potassium-sparing diuretics increase hyperkalemia risk.','Serum creatinine and potassium after initiation or titration.','Many ACE inhibitors are cleared renally; renal function influences dosing.','Contraindicated during pregnancy because of fetal toxicity.','Severe angioedema requires immediate airway assessment and emergency care.');
klass('arb','Angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB)','Blocks angiotensin II at the AT1 receptor, reducing vasoconstriction and aldosterone effects.','Avoid in pregnancy; use caution in bilateral renal artery stenosis.','Hyperkalemia, hypotension, and changes in renal function.','Combining with ACE inhibitors generally increases adverse renal and potassium effects.','Creatinine and potassium after initiation or dose changes.','Losartan has an active metabolite; pharmacokinetics vary across ARBs.','Contraindicated during pregnancy due to fetal toxicity.','Overdose may produce marked hypotension; supportive management is central.');
klass('bb','Beta-1 selective blocker','Blocks cardiac beta-1 receptors, lowering heart rate, contractility and renin secretion.','Caution with marked bradycardia, high-grade AV block or acute decompensated heart failure.','Bradycardia, fatigue, hypotension.','Other AV-nodal blockers can compound bradycardia or conduction block.','Heart rate, blood pressure and symptoms of bradycardia.','Metoprolol is extensively metabolized by CYP2D6; formulations differ.','Selectivity is dose-dependent; consider bronchospastic disease and diabetes context.','Overdose can produce bradycardia and shock requiring urgent resuscitation.');
klass('ccb-dhp','Dihydropyridine calcium channel blocker','Blocks L-type calcium channels predominantly in vascular smooth muscle, causing arteriolar dilation.','Use caution with severe hypotension.','Peripheral edema, flushing and headache.','Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors may increase exposure to some agents.','Blood pressure and peripheral edema.','Amlodipine has a long elimination half-life supporting once-daily use.','Dose cautiously in significant hepatic impairment for applicable agents.','Overdose can cause severe vasodilatory shock.');
klass('ccb-ndhp','Non-dihydropyridine calcium channel blocker','Blocks cardiac L-type calcium channels, slowing AV-node conduction and reducing contractility.','Avoid in significant AV block without a pacemaker and in many patients with HFrEF.','Bradycardia, heart block and constipation (especially verapamil).','Beta blockers can produce additive bradycardia and AV block.','Pulse, blood pressure and ECG when indicated.','Diltiazem and verapamil have important CYP3A4 and P-gp interactions.','May worsen systolic heart failure in susceptible patients.','Severe overdose can cause bradycardia, conduction block and shock.');
klass('thiazide','Thiazide-type diuretic','Inhibits the Na-Cl cotransporter in the distal convoluted tubule.','Use caution with significant electrolyte depletion or gout.','Hyponatremia, hypokalemia, hyperuricemia.','Lithium levels can rise with thiazide coadministration.','Sodium, potassium, creatinine, blood pressure.','Hydrochlorothiazide undergoes renal elimination; chlorthalidone lasts longer.','Older adults have increased susceptibility to hyponatremia.','Marked electrolyte disturbances require urgent correction.');
klass('loop','Loop diuretic','Inhibits NKCC2 in the thick ascending limb of Henle, causing potent natriuresis.','Use caution with hypovolemia, severe electrolyte depletion or anuria depending on agent.','Hypokalemia, metabolic alkalosis, volume depletion and ototoxicity.','Aminoglycosides may increase ototoxicity risk.','Volume status, potassium, magnesium, renal function and daily weights.','Furosemide oral bioavailability is variable compared with torsemide.','Renal function and fluid status affect dose response.','Excess diuresis may cause dehydration and electrolyte emergencies.');
klass('mra','Mineralocorticoid receptor antagonist','Blocks aldosterone receptors in the distal nephron, limiting sodium retention and potassium excretion.','Avoid or use extreme caution with hyperkalemia or significant renal impairment.','Hyperkalemia; spironolactone may cause gynecomastia.','ACE inhibitors, ARBs or potassium supplements raise potassium risk.','Potassium and renal function closely after initiation.','Spironolactone has active metabolites; eplerenone is more receptor-selective.','Kidney dysfunction increases risk of dangerous hyperkalemia.','Severe hyperkalemia can cause arrhythmias requiring emergency treatment.');
klass('statin','HMG-CoA reductase inhibitor (statin)','Inhibits hepatic HMG-CoA reductase, upregulating LDL receptors and lowering LDL cholesterol.','Avoid in active liver disease; most statins are not recommended in pregnancy.','Myalgias, rare rhabdomyolysis and transaminase elevations.','Some CYP3A4 inhibitors increase levels of atorvastatin or simvastatin.','Lipid response and symptoms of muscle toxicity; baseline hepatic assessment.','Atorvastatin is metabolized by CYP3A4; pravastatin has fewer CYP interactions.','Pregnancy requires an individualized assessment and usually discontinuation.','Rhabdomyolysis may lead to acute kidney injury.');
klass('p2y12','P2Y12 platelet inhibitor','Inhibits ADP-mediated P2Y12 platelet activation and aggregation.','Active pathological bleeding is a key contraindication.','Bleeding, bruising; ticagrelor can cause dyspnea.','Other antithrombotics and NSAIDs increase bleeding risk.','Signs of bleeding, CBC as clinically indicated and adherence after stenting.','Clopidogrel requires CYP2C19 bioactivation; genetic variation matters.','Perioperative interruption depends on stent and thrombotic risk.','Major bleeding requires urgent assessment; no universal antidote for this class.');
klass('doac-xa','Direct factor Xa inhibitor','Directly inhibits activated factor X, reducing thrombin generation.','Avoid with active major bleeding; specific restrictions apply in mechanical valves.','Bleeding and anemia.','Strong combined P-gp and CYP3A4 modulators alter levels of some Xa inhibitors.','Renal function, bleeding and appropriate dosing criteria.','Apixaban and rivaroxaban differ in dosing and degree of renal elimination.','Kidney function, age, weight and indication can affect dosing.','Andexanet alfa may be considered for selected life-threatening Xa-inhibitor bleeding; protocols vary.');
klass('warfarin','Vitamin K antagonist','Inhibits VKORC1, reducing production of functional vitamin K-dependent clotting factors.','Contraindicated in most pregnancy circumstances; avoid with active major bleeding.','Bleeding and rare skin necrosis.','Many medications and changes in vitamin K intake affect anticoagulation.','INR and bleeding symptoms; dose is individualized.','Delayed anticoagulant effect reflects clotting factor turnover, not just drug half-life.','Usually avoided in pregnancy due to fetal effects; selected exceptional indications require specialist input.','Vitamin K and four-factor PCC are used for selected severe bleeding scenarios.');
klass('biguanide','Biguanide','Decreases hepatic glucose production and improves insulin sensitivity.','Avoid in severe renal impairment (eGFR <30 mL/min/1.73 m²).','Diarrhea, GI upset and vitamin B12 deficiency.','Iodinated contrast precautions depend on kidney function and clinical context.','Renal function, A1c and periodic B12 in at-risk patients.','Metformin is not metabolized and is eliminated renally.','Temporarily hold in selected acute illness or hypoxic states.','Lactic acidosis is rare but potentially life-threatening.');
klass('insulin','Insulin preparation','Activates insulin receptors to promote glucose uptake and suppress hepatic glucose output.','Hypoglycemia is a major safety concern; dosing must match food and glucose context.','Hypoglycemia, weight gain and hypokalemia.','Other glucose-lowering agents and beta blockers can complicate hypoglycemia risk or recognition.','Blood glucose, hypoglycemia symptoms and potassium in relevant acute settings.','Onset, peak and duration vary widely by insulin formulation.','Dosing must be individualized in children, pregnancy, renal disease and acute illness.','Severe hypoglycemia requires prompt glucose or glucagon therapy.');
klass('glp1','GLP-1 receptor agonist','Activates GLP-1 receptors, enhancing glucose-dependent insulin secretion and satiety.','Avoid with personal/family history of medullary thyroid carcinoma or MEN2 for labeled agents.','Nausea, vomiting, diarrhea and delayed gastric emptying.','Delayed gastric emptying may affect absorption of certain oral medications.','Weight, glucose response and gastrointestinal tolerability.','Long-acting injectable formulations may have weekly administration intervals.','Perioperative planning may need to consider gastric-emptying symptoms and current guidance.','Overdose is mainly supportive, focusing on GI effects and hydration.');
klass('sglt2','SGLT2 inhibitor','Blocks renal proximal-tubule SGLT2, increasing urinary glucose and sodium excretion.','Avoid use for glycemic control in severe kidney dysfunction per agent labeling; caution with ketoacidosis risk.','Genital mycotic infections, volume depletion and euglycemic ketoacidosis.','Diuretics may increase risk of volume depletion.','Renal function, volume status and ketoacidosis symptoms when ill.','Glucose-lowering efficacy decreases as renal filtration declines.','Often held before planned procedures because of ketoacidosis risk; follow agent-specific timing.','Euglycemic DKA may occur despite relatively normal blood glucose.');
klass('ppi','Proton pump inhibitor','Irreversibly inhibits gastric parietal-cell H+/K+-ATPase to suppress acid secretion.','Review indication for long-term use and known hypersensitivity.','Headache, diarrhea and potential long-term electrolyte effects.','Omeprazole can reduce clopidogrel activation through CYP2C19 inhibition.','Symptom response; magnesium or other tests when clinically indicated.','Acid suppression outlasts plasma half-life because pumps are irreversibly inhibited.','Use an appropriate indication and lowest effective duration.','Excessive exposure is usually managed supportively.');
klass('h2','Histamine H2 receptor blocker','Blocks parietal-cell H2 receptors to reduce gastric acid production.','Dose-adjust renally eliminated agents when kidney function is impaired.','Headache and occasionally confusion in susceptible older adults.','Changes in gastric pH can alter absorption of pH-dependent drugs.','Symptom response and renal function when relevant.','Famotidine is predominantly renally eliminated.','Reduce dose in renal impairment, particularly older adults.','Overdose is usually treated supportively.');
klass('nsaid','Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID)','Inhibits cyclooxygenase enzymes, lowering prostaglandin synthesis.','Avoid with active GI bleeding; caution with renal disease, cardiovascular risk and late pregnancy.','GI ulceration or bleeding, renal injury and fluid retention.','Anticoagulants and antiplatelets increase bleeding risk.','Pain relief, renal function, blood pressure and bleeding symptoms.','Agents differ in COX selectivity and elimination half-life.','Avoid NSAIDs at 20 weeks or later in pregnancy unless specifically advised by a clinician.','Overdose may cause GI and renal toxicity; severe cases need emergency evaluation.');
klass('apap','Non-opioid analgesic / antipyretic','Acts centrally to reduce pain and fever; its full analgesic mechanism remains incompletely understood.','Use particular caution in significant hepatic disease and with combination products.','Generally well tolerated at recommended doses; hepatotoxicity in overdose.','Chronic heavy alcohol use and multiple acetaminophen products raise liver injury risk.','Total daily acetaminophen from all products and liver tests when indicated.','Predominantly hepatic metabolism with a small toxic NAPQI pathway.','Weight, liver disease and formulation influence safe dosing.','N-acetylcysteine is the antidote for clinically significant acetaminophen toxicity.');
klass('opioid','Mu-opioid receptor agonist','Stimulates mu-opioid receptors to produce analgesia and respiratory depression.','Avoid or use extreme caution in significant respiratory depression and with sedatives.','Respiratory depression, constipation, sedation and nausea.','Benzodiazepines and alcohol increase risk of profound sedation and respiratory depression.','Respiratory rate, sedation, pain response and bowel function.','Onset and duration differ by route and formulation; many agents have active metabolites.','Older adults, sleep apnea and renal dysfunction increase susceptibility to adverse effects.','Naloxone can reverse opioid-induced respiratory depression; repeated doses may be needed.');
klass('aminopen','Aminopenicillin beta-lactam antibiotic','Binds penicillin-binding proteins and inhibits bacterial cell-wall cross-linking.','Serious immediate beta-lactam hypersensitivity is a key concern.','Rash, diarrhea and hypersensitivity reactions.','Allopurinol can increase aminopenicillin-associated rash incidence.','Clinical response, allergy symptoms and renal function when indicated.','Primarily renal elimination; dose adjustments may be needed.','Pediatric dosing is weight- and indication-dependent.','Severe allergy/anaphylaxis warrants emergency management.');
klass('ceph3','Third-generation cephalosporin','Inhibits bacterial cell-wall synthesis by binding penicillin-binding proteins.','History of severe cephalosporin hypersensitivity requires careful assessment.','Diarrhea, biliary precipitation with ceftriaxone and allergic reactions.','Ceftriaxone is incompatible with IV calcium-containing solutions in neonates.','Clinical response and renal/hepatic context as relevant.','Ceftriaxone has both renal and biliary elimination.','Special neonatal precautions apply to ceftriaxone.','Severe immediate hypersensitivity requires emergency care.');
klass('macrolide','Macrolide antibiotic','Binds the bacterial 50S ribosomal subunit, inhibiting protein synthesis.','Use caution with QT prolongation or interacting rhythm medications.','GI upset, QT prolongation and rarely hepatic injury.','Some macrolides inhibit CYP3A4 and interact with statins.','Clinical response and QT-risk factors.','Azithromycin has prolonged tissue persistence and a long terminal half-life.','Age and co-medications inform QT-risk assessment.','Overdose can cause GI and cardiac adverse effects.');
klass('tetracycline','Tetracycline antibiotic','Binds the bacterial 30S ribosomal subunit and blocks tRNA attachment.','Generally avoid during pregnancy and in children younger than 8 unless specifically indicated.','Photosensitivity, esophagitis and GI upset.','Calcium, iron and antacids impair oral absorption.','Clinical response and signs of esophagitis/photosensitivity.','Doxycycline has substantial nonrenal elimination.','Pregnancy and developing teeth require specific consideration.','Overdose is usually managed supportively.');
klass('fluoroquinolone','Fluoroquinolone antibiotic','Inhibits bacterial DNA gyrase and topoisomerase IV.','Avoid routine use when safer options suffice due to serious adverse-effect warnings.','Tendinopathy, neuropathy, QT prolongation (some agents) and dysglycemia.','Antacids and iron reduce oral absorption; QT drugs can compound risk.','Clinical response and tendon, neurologic or glucose symptoms.','Renal dose adjustment is needed for many agents.','Use caution in myasthenia gravis and in pregnancy/pediatrics when alternatives exist.','Severe neurologic or tendon symptoms require stopping the drug and evaluation.');
klass('tmp-smx','Folate-synthesis inhibitor combination','Sequentially blocks bacterial folate synthesis via dihydropteroate synthase and dihydrofolate reductase.','Avoid with serious sulfonamide allergy; caution with renal disease.','Rash, hyperkalemia and cytopenias.','Warfarin anticoagulant effect may increase; ACE inhibitors add hyperkalemia risk.','CBC, potassium and renal function when clinically indicated.','Both components have significant renal handling.','Pregnancy timing and neonatal age influence use.','Severe skin reactions require immediate discontinuation and care.');
klass('glycopep','Glycopeptide antibiotic','Binds D-Ala-D-Ala peptidoglycan precursors, inhibiting cell-wall synthesis.','Use caution with significant renal impairment and infusion reactions.','Nephrotoxicity and infusion-related flushing.','Other nephrotoxic drugs increase kidney injury risk.','Renal function and AUC-guided therapeutic monitoring when indicated.','IV vancomycin is renally cleared; oral vancomycin is minimally absorbed.','Dose/monitor carefully in renal impairment.','Infusion reactions are managed by stopping or slowing infusion and assessment.');
klass('nitroimidazole','Nitroimidazole antimicrobial','Forms reactive intermediates that damage DNA in susceptible anaerobes and protozoa.','Assess severe hepatic impairment and relevant neurologic adverse effects.','Metallic taste, nausea and rarely peripheral neuropathy.','May increase warfarin anticoagulation effect.','Clinical response; neurologic symptoms if prolonged treatment.','Metronidazole is extensively metabolized hepatically.','Dose assessment may be needed in severe hepatic impairment.','Large exposures can produce neurologic toxicity.');
klass('nitrofuran','Urinary antiseptic antibiotic','Bacterial reduction products damage multiple microbial targets; concentrates in urine.','Avoid in significant renal dysfunction per current labeling and at term pregnancy.','Nausea, rare pulmonary or hepatic reactions and neuropathy.','Magnesium trisilicate antacids can impair absorption.','Response of lower UTI symptoms; renal function when relevant.','Therapeutic tissue concentrations are inadequate for pyelonephritis.','Not appropriate for pyelonephritis; special restrictions in late pregnancy.','Chronic pulmonary or liver toxicity warrants prompt discontinuation.');
klass('saba','Short-acting beta-2 agonist','Stimulates airway beta-2 receptors, relaxing bronchial smooth muscle.','Use caution with significant tachyarrhythmia or severe hypokalemia.','Tremor, tachycardia and hypokalemia.','Nonselective beta blockers can antagonize bronchodilation.','Symptoms, rescue-inhaler frequency, heart rate and peak flow where used.','Inhaled albuterol has rapid onset and relatively short duration.','Frequent reliance indicates a need to reassess asthma control.','Excess dosing can cause tachyarrhythmia and hypokalemia.');
klass('ics','Inhaled corticosteroid','Activates glucocorticoid receptors to suppress airway inflammation.','Not a substitute for rapid relief of acute severe bronchospasm.','Oropharyngeal candidiasis and dysphonia.','Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors can increase systemic exposure for some agents.','Asthma control, inhaler technique and oral candidiasis.','Anti-inflammatory benefit develops with regular use, not immediate bronchodilation.','Use spacer/rinse mouth when indicated; assess growth in children.','Excessive systemic exposure can suppress the HPA axis.');
klass('antihist','Second-generation H1 antihistamine','Blocks peripheral H1 histamine receptors to reduce allergic symptoms.','Use caution with renal impairment for renally cleared agents.','Headache, dry mouth and occasional somnolence.','Other sedatives may add to drowsiness with more sedating agents.','Allergic symptom control and sedation.','Cetirizine has prominent renal elimination; many agents are once daily.','Renal dose considerations for cetirizine.','Overdose is generally supportive; excess sedation may occur.');
klass('epi','Adrenergic agonist (alpha and beta)','Activates alpha-1, beta-1 and beta-2 receptors, reversing vasodilation and bronchospasm.','In life-threatening anaphylaxis there is no absolute contraindication to IM epinephrine.','Palpitations, tremor and tachycardia.','Nonselective beta blockade may alter response to epinephrine.','Airway, breathing, perfusion and repeat treatment needs in emergency use.','Rapid metabolism by COMT and MAO; clinical effects are short lived.','IM epinephrine is first-line for anaphylaxis across age groups with weight-based device selection.','Excess exposure can cause serious tachyarrhythmias or hypertension.');
klass('ssri','Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SSRI)','Blocks serotonin transporter (SERT), increasing synaptic serotonin.','Avoid with MAO inhibitors; screen for bipolar disorder before antidepressant monotherapy.','GI upset, sexual dysfunction and activation early in therapy.','MAO inhibitors and other serotonergic drugs increase serotonin-syndrome risk.','Mood, suicidality when indicated, tolerability and adherence.','Clinical antidepressant effects often take weeks despite immediate transporter blockade.','Monitor young patients closely for emerging suicidal thoughts; pregnancy decisions are individualized.','Serotonin syndrome presents with neuromuscular hyperactivity, autonomic changes and mental-status changes.');
klass('snri','Serotonin–norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor (SNRI)','Inhibits serotonin and norepinephrine transporters, increasing both neurotransmitters.','Avoid MAO inhibitors and use caution with uncontrolled hypertension for some agents.','Nausea, sexual dysfunction, sweating and blood-pressure elevation.','Other serotonergic agents increase serotonin-syndrome risk.','Mood, blood pressure, adverse effects and discontinuation symptoms.','Venlafaxine has a clinically important active metabolite.','Kidney or liver impairment may change dosing for certain agents.','Toxicity can include serotonin syndrome and cardiovascular effects.');
klass('bup','Norepinephrine–dopamine reuptake inhibitor','Inhibits norepinephrine and dopamine reuptake without direct serotonin reuptake blockade.','Contraindicated in seizure disorders and current/prior bulimia or anorexia nervosa.','Insomnia, dry mouth, anxiety and dose-related seizures.','Other seizure-threshold-lowering drugs may increase seizure risk.','Mood, sleep, blood pressure and seizure risk.','CYP2B6 forms active metabolites; formulation affects release.','Use caution with conditions that lower seizure threshold.','Overdose can cause delayed seizures and cardiac toxicity.');
klass('atypical','Second-generation antipsychotic','Modulates dopamine D2 and serotonin 5-HT2A signaling, with agent-specific receptor activity.','Use caution in elderly patients with dementia-related psychosis and metabolic risk.','Weight gain, metabolic syndrome and extrapyramidal symptoms (vary by agent).','Other QT-prolonging or sedating drugs can compound risk.','Weight/BMI, A1c/glucose, lipids and movement symptoms.','Metabolism and half-life vary greatly among agents.','Older adults with dementia-related psychosis carry increased mortality warning.','Overdose may cause sedation, hypotension and rhythm changes.');
klass('benzo','Benzodiazepine','Positive allosteric modulator of GABA-A receptors, increasing chloride-channel opening frequency.','Use caution or avoid with respiratory compromise, opioids or high fall risk.','Sedation, falls, respiratory depression and dependence.','Opioids and alcohol synergistically depress respiration and consciousness.','Sedation, respiration and dependence/withdrawal risk.','Agent half-lives and active metabolites vary considerably.','Older adults are particularly sensitive to confusion and falls.','Flumazenil has limited, carefully selected use because it can precipitate seizures.');
klass('lithium','Mood stabilizer (lithium)','Alters intracellular signaling pathways; precise mood-stabilizing mechanism is multifactorial.','Avoid or closely manage in dehydration, significant renal impairment and certain pregnancy contexts.','Tremor, hypothyroidism, nephrogenic diabetes insipidus.','NSAIDs, ACE inhibitors and thiazides can raise lithium levels.','Trough lithium levels, creatinine, TSH and electrolytes.','Renally excreted unchanged with a narrow therapeutic index.','Volume depletion and pregnancy-related renal changes alter lithium handling.','Toxicity causes GI symptoms, coarse tremor, ataxia and neurologic changes.');
klass('antiepileptic-sv2a','SV2A-binding antiseizure medication','Binds synaptic vesicle protein SV2A, modifying neurotransmitter release.','Use caution with significant behavioral adverse effects or renal impairment.','Somnolence, dizziness and irritability or behavioral changes.','Relatively few CYP-mediated drug interactions.','Seizure frequency, mood/behavior and renal function.','Levetiracetam is mostly renally eliminated.','Renal dose adjustment is usually necessary.','Overdose mainly causes CNS depression and behavioral symptoms.');
klass('antiepileptic-na','Sodium-channel-modulating antiseizure medication','Inhibits voltage-gated sodium channels and reduces excessive neuronal firing.','Avoid restarting at a high dose after significant interruption because of rash risk.','Rash, dizziness and rare Stevens–Johnson syndrome.','Valproate inhibits lamotrigine metabolism, substantially increasing exposure.','Rash, seizure or mood control and adherence to titration schedule.','Primarily glucuronidated; estrogen-containing contraceptives may lower levels.','Pregnancy and hormonal contraception can alter lamotrigine concentrations.','Serious rash warrants urgent clinical assessment.');
klass('propofol','Intravenous general anesthetic','Potentiates GABA-A receptor activity, producing rapid hypnosis without analgesia.','Requires airway, ventilatory and hemodynamic monitoring by trained clinicians.','Hypotension, apnea and pain on injection.','Opioids and other sedatives increase cardiorespiratory depression.','Airway, ventilation, oxygenation, blood pressure and depth of anesthesia.','Rapid onset and redistribution contribute to short duration after bolus.','Hemodynamic effects are more pronounced in frail or hypovolemic patients.','Prolonged high-dose infusion can cause rare propofol infusion syndrome.');
klass('volatile','Volatile inhalational anesthetic','Modulates multiple neuronal targets to produce unconsciousness and immobility.','Malignant hyperthermia susceptibility is an important contraindication.','Hypotension, nausea and malignant hyperthermia in susceptible patients.','Other anesthetics produce additive CNS and cardiorespiratory effects.','End-tidal anesthetic concentration, ventilation and hemodynamics.','Low blood:gas solubility permits relatively rapid adjustments for sevoflurane.','Special caution with malignant hyperthermia susceptibility.','Malignant hyperthermia requires stopping triggering agents and prompt dantrolene.');
klass('nmba-nondep','Nondepolarizing neuromuscular blocker','Competitively antagonizes nicotinic acetylcholine receptors at the neuromuscular junction.','Does not provide hypnosis or analgesia; ensure adequate sedation/anesthesia.','Residual paralysis and rare anaphylaxis.','Aminoglycosides and magnesium can potentiate blockade.','Quantitative train-of-four and airway/ventilation status.','Rocuronium is primarily cleared hepatobiliary with variable duration.','Organ dysfunction can prolong neuromuscular blockade.','Residual block can cause respiratory failure; use appropriate reversal and ventilation.');
klass('nmba-dep','Depolarizing neuromuscular blocker','Persistently depolarizes nicotinic receptors at the motor endplate, producing paralysis.','Avoid with known malignant hyperthermia susceptibility or risk of severe hyperkalemia.','Hyperkalemia, bradycardia, fasciculations and malignant hyperthermia.','Other agents affecting neuromuscular function may alter clinical effects.','Airway, ventilation and neuromuscular function.','Succinylcholine is rapidly hydrolyzed by plasma butyrylcholinesterase.','Burns, denervation or neuromuscular disease can increase hyperkalemia risk.','Malignant hyperthermia requires dantrolene; severe hyperkalemia needs emergency treatment.');
klass('sugammadex','Selective relaxant-binding agent','Encapsulates rocuronium or vecuronium, lowering free neuromuscular blocker concentration.','Use caution in severe renal impairment and with hypersensitivity history.','Bradycardia, hypersensitivity and nausea.','Can reduce efficacy of hormonal contraceptives; provide backup counseling per label.','Recovery of neuromuscular function with quantitative monitoring.','Eliminated renally as a sugammadex–blocker complex.','Not recommended in severe renal impairment under product labeling.','Severe bradycardia or anaphylaxis requires immediate treatment.');
klass('5ht3','5-HT3 receptor antagonist','Blocks serotonin 5-HT3 receptors centrally and peripherally to reduce nausea and vomiting.','Use caution in congenital long-QT syndrome and with other QT-prolonging drugs.','Headache, constipation and QT prolongation.','Other QT-prolonging agents can increase arrhythmia risk.','Symptom response and ECG/electrolytes in high-risk settings.','Ondansetron undergoes hepatic metabolism.','Severe hepatic impairment limits total daily ondansetron dose.','Overdose can cause QT prolongation and cardiac conduction abnormalities.');
klass('naloxone','Opioid receptor antagonist','Competitively displaces opioids from mu receptors, reversing opioid-mediated respiratory depression.','No absolute contraindication when treating suspected life-threatening opioid overdose.','Precipitated withdrawal, agitation, nausea and sympathetic activation.','Long-acting opioids may outlast naloxone, requiring repeat doses.','Ventilation, level of consciousness and recurrence of respiratory depression.','Naloxone has a shorter duration than many opioids.','Opioid-dependent patients may develop acute withdrawal; emergency care remains essential.','Naloxone treats opioid toxicity rather than producing the toxicity itself.');
klass('local-anes','Amide local anesthetic','Blocks voltage-gated sodium channels in nerves, preventing action-potential propagation.','Avoid inadvertent intravascular injection; assess allergies and systemic toxicity risks.','Perioral numbness, tinnitus, seizures or arrhythmia with systemic toxicity.','Other local anesthetics can have additive systemic toxicity.','Injection technique, neurologic symptoms and cardiac status when relevant.','Lidocaine undergoes hepatic metabolism.','Hepatic dysfunction and tissue vascularity alter systemic exposure.','Local anesthetic systemic toxicity requires emergency support and lipid emulsion per protocol.');
klass('uterotonic','Oxytocin receptor agonist','Activates uterine oxytocin receptors, increasing coordinated myometrial contraction.','Requires indication-specific dosing and fetal/uterine monitoring during labor induction.','Uterine tachysystole, hypotension and water intoxication with high exposure.','Other uterotonics may augment uterine activity.','Uterine contractions, fetal heart rate during labor and maternal hemodynamics.','Oxytocin has a short circulating half-life, permitting rapid titration.','Obstetric use depends heavily on gestational and delivery context.','Excess uterine stimulation can compromise fetal oxygenation.');
klass('mag','Magnesium sulfate','Reduces neuromuscular excitability; used for seizure prophylaxis in preeclampsia and for certain arrhythmias.','Use caution with significant renal impairment or myasthenia gravis.','Flushing, reduced reflexes and respiratory depression at toxic levels.','Neuromuscular blockers may have enhanced effects.','Respiratory rate, deep tendon reflexes, urine output and serum magnesium when indicated.','Eliminated by the kidneys, so impaired renal function increases accumulation risk.','Obstetric dosing is protocol-dependent and requires maternal monitoring.','Calcium gluconate is used for clinically significant magnesium toxicity.');
klass('glucocort','Systemic glucocorticoid','Binds intracellular glucocorticoid receptors and changes inflammatory gene transcription.','Use caution in active untreated infections and chronic immunosuppression.','Hyperglycemia, insomnia, fluid retention and long-term osteoporosis.','NSAIDs increase GI bleeding risk; vaccines may require review with immunosuppression.','Blood glucose, blood pressure, infection risk and long-term bone health.','Genomic anti-inflammatory actions take time; potency/duration differ by agent.','Long-term therapy must generally be tapered to protect against adrenal insufficiency.','Abrupt withdrawal after prolonged use can precipitate adrenal crisis.');
klass('alpha1','Alpha-1 adrenergic blocker','Blocks alpha-1 receptors in prostate and bladder-neck smooth muscle, improving urinary flow.','Use caution in orthostatic hypotension and with PDE5 inhibitors.','Dizziness, orthostatic hypotension and ejaculatory changes.','PDE5 inhibitors can increase symptomatic hypotension.','Urinary symptoms, blood pressure and dizziness.','Tamsulosin is metabolized hepatically, including CYP3A4 and CYP2D6.','Older adults are susceptible to orthostasis and falls.','Overdose can cause clinically important hypotension.');
klass('thyroid','Thyroid hormone replacement','Supplies synthetic T4, converted in tissues to active T3.','Avoid using as a weight-loss drug in euthyroid patients.','Excess replacement causes palpitations, arrhythmia and bone loss.','Iron, calcium and certain foods impair absorption if taken together.','TSH (and free T4 in select circumstances) after dose changes.','Levothyroxine has a long half-life and delayed steady-state response.','Pregnancy often increases levothyroxine requirements; monitor thyroid tests.','Overdose causes manifestations of thyrotoxicosis.');
klass('antithyroid','Thionamide antithyroid medication','Inhibits thyroid peroxidase, reducing thyroid hormone synthesis.','Serious prior agranulocytosis or significant hepatic injury warrants avoidance.','Rash, rare agranulocytosis and hepatotoxicity.','Changing thyroid status can alter warfarin requirements.','Free T4/T3 during titration and fever/sore-throat warning symptoms.','Effect on thyroid hormone levels is delayed by stored hormone.','PTU is often preferred over methimazole in early first trimester when needed.','Fever or sore throat may signal agranulocytosis and requires urgent CBC evaluation.');
klass('coc','Combined hormonal contraceptive','Estrogen suppresses FSH and progestin suppresses LH surge, preventing ovulation.','Avoid with migraine with aura or current high-risk thromboembolic conditions.','Nausea, breast tenderness and increased venous thrombosis risk.','Enzyme-inducing antiseizure drugs can reduce contraceptive effectiveness.','Blood pressure and major thrombotic risk factors.','Oral formulations require adherence and undergo hepatic metabolism.','Smoking at age ≥35 and certain migraine patterns affect eligibility.','Serious thromboembolic symptoms require urgent evaluation.');
klass('progestin','Progestin contraceptive','Thickens cervical mucus and, depending on product, inhibits ovulation.','Use product-specific guidance for current breast cancer or unexplained bleeding.','Irregular bleeding, headache and nausea.','Strong hepatic enzyme inducers can reduce effectiveness of some products.','Bleeding patterns, pregnancy concerns and adherence/product timing.','Levonorgestrel emergency contraception is most effective when taken promptly.','Emergency contraception does not treat an established pregnancy.','Overdose commonly causes nausea and bleeding changes.');
klass('gnrh','GnRH agonist','Continuous GnRH receptor stimulation downregulates pituitary gonadotropin release after an initial flare.','Caution with pregnancy and conditions worsened by initial hormone flare.','Hot flashes, reduced bone density and initial symptom flare.','Other QT-prolonging medications may add risk for some formulations.','Symptoms, hormone suppression and bone health with prolonged treatment.','Long-acting depot preparations suppress sex steroids after an initial flare.','Bone effects and fertility implications merit counseling.','Overexposure causes profound sex-steroid suppression.');


klass('ceph1','First-generation cephalosporin','Binds bacterial penicillin-binding proteins to inhibit cell-wall cross-linking; strong MSSA and streptococcal activity.','Serious cephalosporin hypersensitivity requires careful assessment.','Diarrhea, hypersensitivity reactions and rarely C. difficile infection.','Concurrent nephrotoxic medications may increase renal safety concerns in susceptible patients.','Perioperative timing, allergy history and renal function when applicable.','Cefazolin is renally eliminated and may need adjustment in renal impairment.','Weight, procedure, renal function and redosing intervals matter for surgical prophylaxis.','Severe immediate hypersensitivity requires emergency care.');
klass('lmwh','Low-molecular-weight heparin (LMWH)','Potentiates antithrombin to inhibit factor Xa more than factor IIa.','Active major bleeding and prior heparin-induced thrombocytopenia are key restrictions.','Bleeding, injection-site bruising and less frequent HIT than unfractionated heparin.','Other anticoagulants or antiplatelets increase bleeding risk.','CBC/platelets when indicated, renal function, bleeding; anti-Xa only in selected situations.','Enoxaparin undergoes substantial renal elimination, requiring adjustment with renal impairment.','Body weight, kidney function, pregnancy and timing around neuraxial procedures matter.','Protamine only partially reverses enoxaparin anticoagulant effects.');
klass('ufh','Unfractionated heparin','Potentiates antithrombin, inhibiting thrombin (IIa) and factor Xa.','Active major bleeding or current/history of immune HIT are important contraindications.','Bleeding and heparin-induced thrombocytopenia.','Concurrent anticoagulants or antiplatelets amplify bleeding risk.','aPTT or anti-Xa as protocol-directed for infusions; platelet counts and bleeding.','Short half-life and rapid titratability of IV infusion, with variable binding.','Often useful when rapid offset is needed or renal function is very poor.','Protamine sulfate can reverse unfractionated heparin.');
klass('ketamine','Dissociative anesthetic (NMDA antagonist)','Noncompetitively antagonizes NMDA receptors, producing dissociation and analgesia.','Use caution with conditions where increased sympathetic stimulation is harmful.','Emergence reactions, increased secretions, hypertension and tachycardia.','Other sedatives may increase respiratory or CNS depression.','Airway, respiratory status, hemodynamics and emergence phenomena.','Ketamine has active metabolites and undergoes hepatic metabolism.','Airway monitoring remains necessary even though spontaneous breathing may be relatively preserved.','Severe toxicity requires supportive airway and cardiovascular management.');
klass('dexmed','Alpha-2 adrenergic agonist sedative','Stimulates central alpha-2 receptors, reducing sympathetic outflow and providing sedation.','Use caution in significant bradycardia, hypotension and conduction disease.','Bradycardia, hypotension and occasionally transient hypertension during loading.','Beta blockers and other bradycardic drugs can intensify heart-rate effects.','Heart rate, blood pressure, sedation depth and airway status.','Hepatic metabolism and context-dependent effects influence infusion recovery.','Dose cautiously in hepatic impairment and hemodynamically unstable patients.','Overdose can lead to pronounced bradycardia and hypotension.');
klass('ergot-uterotonic','Ergot-derived uterotonic','Activates uterine smooth muscle receptors to increase sustained uterine contraction.','Contraindicated in hypertension and preeclampsia due to vasoconstrictive effects.','Hypertension, nausea and vasospasm.','Other vasoconstrictors can intensify hypertension.','Blood pressure and uterine tone after administration.','Methylergonovine is not the preferred agent for labor induction.','Avoid in hypertensive disorders of pregnancy.','Excess exposure can cause severe hypertension and vascular ischemia.');
klass('pge1','Prostaglandin E1 analogue','Activates prostaglandin receptors, promoting cervical ripening and uterine contraction and protecting gastric mucosa in other contexts.','Indication-specific pregnancy precautions are essential; obstetric regimens differ widely.','Cramping, diarrhea, fever and uterine tachysystole.','Other uterotonics can intensify uterine stimulation.','Uterine activity and maternal/fetal status when used for obstetric indications.','Misoprostol is converted to active misoprostol acid.','Routes and doses vary greatly among obstetric and nonobstetric uses.','Excess uterine activity may cause serious maternal or fetal complications.');
klass('pgf2','Prostaglandin F2-alpha analogue','Stimulates uterine smooth muscle contraction through prostaglandin FP receptors.','Avoid in patients with asthma because it can precipitate bronchospasm.','Diarrhea, fever, vomiting and bronchospasm.','Other uterotonics may have additive uterine effects.','Uterine tone, bleeding and respiratory status.','Carboprost is administered parenterally under obstetric protocols.','Particularly important to screen for asthma before use.','Excess exposure may cause severe bronchospasm or uterine hyperstimulation.');
klass('gabapentinoid','Gabapentinoid (alpha-2-delta calcium-channel ligand)','Binds alpha-2-delta subunits of presynaptic voltage-gated calcium channels, reducing excitatory neurotransmitter release.','Use caution with respiratory compromise, sedation risk and renal impairment.','Somnolence, dizziness and peripheral edema.','Opioids and other sedatives increase respiratory depression risk.','Sedation, dizziness, renal function and symptom response.','Gabapentin and pregabalin are eliminated mainly unchanged by kidneys.','Renal adjustment and fall risk matter, especially in older adults.','Overdose can cause marked CNS depression; supportive care is central.');
klass('lincosamide','Lincosamide antibiotic','Binds bacterial 50S ribosomal subunit and inhibits protein synthesis.','History of antibiotic-associated colitis warrants caution.','Diarrhea and elevated risk of C. difficile infection.','Neuromuscular blocking agents can have additive effects.','Clinical response and significant diarrhea symptoms.','Clindamycin is predominantly hepatically metabolized.','Route and susceptibility guide use for skin and anaerobic infections.','Severe antibiotic-associated colitis may be life-threatening.');
klass('antipseudopen','Antipseudomonal penicillin with beta-lactamase inhibitor','Piperacillin inhibits cell-wall synthesis and tazobactam inhibits susceptible beta-lactamases.','Severe immediate penicillin allergy is an important contraindication.','Diarrhea, hypersensitivity and kidney injury risk in certain combinations.','Co-administration with vancomycin may increase AKI risk in some settings.','Renal function, cultures, clinical response and allergic reactions.','Substantial renal elimination requires dose changes in renal impairment.','Hospital dosing often depends on infusion strategy and renal function.','Severe allergy and toxicity require discontinuation and supportive care.');
klass('ceph4','Fourth-generation cephalosporin','Inhibits cell-wall synthesis and has broad gram-negative activity including susceptible Pseudomonas.','Cephalosporin hypersensitivity and renal impairment require assessment.','Neurotoxicity, especially encephalopathy or seizures when accumulation occurs.','Other neurotoxic agents may increase neurologic risk.','Kidney function, cultures and changes in mental status.','Cefepime is predominantly renally eliminated.','Renal dose adjustment is essential to limit neurotoxicity.','Cefepime accumulation can cause encephalopathy or seizures.');
klass('na-inhib','Neuraminidase inhibitor antiviral','Inhibits influenza viral neuraminidase, impairing release of newly formed virions.','Use with attention to renal function and indicated influenza context.','Nausea and vomiting.','Few major CYP-mediated drug interactions.','Symptom course and treatment timing in appropriate patients.','Oseltamivir is converted to an active metabolite cleared by the kidneys.','Dose adjustment is needed in some renal impairment; benefit is greatest when started promptly.','Overdose generally produces gastrointestinal symptoms.');
klass('nucleoside-antiviral','Guansine nucleoside analogue antiviral','After viral kinase activation, inhibits viral DNA polymerase and DNA replication.','Use caution in significant renal impairment and dehydration.','Nausea, headache and crystal-associated kidney injury with some IV regimens.','Other nephrotoxins increase kidney injury risk.','Renal function and hydration, especially with IV therapy.','Acyclovir is primarily renally excreted.','Renal dose adjustments are often needed.','High exposure with renal dysfunction can produce neurotoxicity.');
klass('azole','Triazole antifungal','Inhibits fungal lanosterol 14-alpha-demethylase, decreasing ergosterol synthesis.','Use caution with hepatic disease and QT-prolongation risk.','Liver enzyme elevations, GI upset and QT prolongation.','CYP inhibition can raise exposure to warfarin and some statins.','Liver tests when appropriate, interactions and clinical response.','Fluconazole has high oral bioavailability and predominantly renal clearance.','Pregnancy exposure and renal dosing require careful indication-specific evaluation.','Significant overdose can produce hallucinations and arrhythmias.');
klass('txa','Antifibrinolytic (tranexamic acid)','Competitively inhibits plasminogen activation and plasmin binding to fibrin, reducing clot breakdown.','Avoid in active intravascular clotting; indication-specific thrombotic assessment matters.','Nausea, thrombotic concerns and seizures with high IV exposure.','Concurrent prothrombotic therapies require careful risk assessment.','Bleeding response, thrombosis signs and renal function.','Tranexamic acid is largely eliminated unchanged in urine.','Dose modification may be needed in renal impairment.','High IV exposures can cause seizures, requiring immediate assessment.');

